4 appears on the river, you would complete a straight (2-3-4-5-6). The board is dangerous because there are three clubs, meaning a flush is possible for your opponent. Since your opponent has checked to you, you have the opportunity to see the final card for free.\n\nReason: Betting would be risky because the opponent might call with a club (drawing to a flush) or any pair, and you have no showdown value if called. Taking the free card (Check) maximizes your efficiency by giving you a chance to hit your straight without investing more chips into a pot where you are currently behind.\n\nAnswer: 0'}
