 the river card for free, controlling the size of the pot. My hand is strong enough to win at showdown often, but not strong enough to build a massive pot against a potential Trip Queens or Straight.\n\nSo, I'm going to **check (0)**.\n\n\n", 'output': 'Evaluation: You hold 10 of Diamonds and 7 of Hearts on a board of 10h, Qd, 9h, Qc. This gives you Two Pair (Queens and Tens) with a 9 kicker. The opponent has checked through the Pre-flop and Flop rounds, indicating weakness or a slow-played monster. Given the small pot size and the paired board (which introduces risks of Trips) and straight possibilities (connected 9-10-Q), your hand has good showdown value but is vulnerable. Checking controls the pot size and allows you to reach the showdown cheaply or induce a bluff on the River.\n\nReason: Your Two Pair is likely the best hand currently, but betting risks reopening the action to a raise from a hidden Trip Queens or a made Straight. Checking keeps the pot small, consistent with the marginal strength of Two Pair on a paired board, and denies the opponent the chance to bluff-raise you off your hand on the Turn.\n\nAnswer: 0'}
